> I am looking for a hack-version for a pc that has graphic symbols
> instead   of the characters. I once had such a game running on my old
> amiga, but I   have been unable to find a ibm-version. I know there
> does exist a SSI role-  playing game called "Hack", but that doesn't
> have to do anything with the   great original game.
> Could someone please help me? Where can I ftp such a game?

ftp to ftp.uml.edu
in the directory /msdos/Games/Utils, you will find a file called
chrrhac23.zip.

Download it
Read the DOCS included in the file
set it up
play nethack  :)

This is not a memory resident program, so will not cause any memory
problems.  It simply changes the DOS font and your NETHACK.CNF file so
that the monsters, symbols, and objects are all in the charecters not
used by the alphanumeric charecters.



